          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best protein powder with probiotics is one that would be worth buying without them. Garden of Life Sport Organic Plant-Based Protein clears that bar, and it adds a named spore-forming strain at a disclosed 2 billion CFU dose with NSF Certified for Sport testing. Vega offers the same strain at a higher price, and Momentous is the cleanest whey option if enzymes are what you want.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep expectations realistic. Probiotic effects are strain-specific, fragile bacteria fade in an opened tub, and enzyme research mostly shows small changes in blood amino acids rather than better digestion. If you have a specific gut goal, buy a separate probiotic with evidence for that goal and choose your protein powder on its own merits.
